## Acceptance mapping
- assetManifest v17 schema: manifestVersion const 17, generatedAt RFC3339, assets[] with exerciseId/glbPath/thumb512Path/heroPath/sha256/sizeBytes/version/draco; glbPath pattern enforces '/assets/exercises/<id>/movement.v<N>.<sha256-12>.glb'
- modelManifest schema (blueprint p.769): manifestVersion, models[]{name, version, schemaVersion, minAppVersion, sha256, url, rollout}
- Validator checks: required fields, sha256 hex format, content-addressed path == sha256[:12], version int>=1 (+ cross-field version-in-path, dir==exerciseId, unique ids); exit 0/1 with reasons
- Cache rules documented in wrangler.toml.example comment block: manifests 'public,max-age=60'; hashed GLBs/WebPs 'public,max-age=31536000,immutable'
- README documents wrangler install, account+zone signup, bucket create, custom domain connect, cache rule clicks, R2 API token for CI, CI upload pattern, and cost note (10GB free tier, ~<1GB expected footprint, zero egress)
- NOT DONE BY DESIGN (requires user account): bucket creation, domain connection, cache rule creation, any upload. Downstream todos 25 (upload pipeline) and 27 (client SHA256 validation) consume these schemas.
